  M20 is why the LOW 2 code change was REVERTED rather than kept. A first pass
  reordered assertPostablePeriod to read the period status first and create the
  year only on `no_period`, with a test asserting a closed-period refusal writes
  no fiscal_periods rows. That test passed on the UNMUTATED original too — it
  proved nothing. The reason is that ensureFiscalPeriodForDate returns early
  whenever a covering period exists, and its lookup (getFiscalPeriodIdForDate,
  fiscalPeriodService.ts:110) does NOT filter on status, so the closed path
  never wrote in the first place. No behaviour separates the two versions on any
  input, so the change was reverted, the vacuous test deleted, and the doc
  comment corrected to state the actual reason the invariant holds. Recorded
  rather than left as an unkillable production change.

